        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Crawl space encapsulation typically costs roughly $5,000 to $15,000 for an average home, with simple liner-and-dehumidifier jobs at the low end and drainage, mold work or structural repairs pushing totals much higher. Prices vary by region and change over time, so use these ranges to judge quotes rather than to budget to the dollar.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Spend money in order: fix gutters and grading, measure humidity and wood moisture, deal with any water or mold, then seal and condition the space. Insist on itemized quotes and before-and-after readings. Done that way, encapsulation is one of the better investments in a humid climate, and you will know exactly what you paid for.
          </p>
